          </p>
          <p>
            Whatever you use, keep it loaded but not dripping, maintain a wet edge, and never overwork the finish once it starts to set. For a deeper dive on choosing applicators, see our dedicated guide to the <a href="/best-brush-for-water-based-polyurethane" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-medium">best brush for water-based polyurethane</a>.
