              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is water-based polyurethane better than oil-based for floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Water-based poly dries crystal-clear and stays clear, while oil-based dries amber and yellows over time. Water-based is also low-odor, low-VOC, and dries fast (2-4 hour recoat). Oil-based is more durable per coat, but water-based catches up with an extra coat. For light and grey-toned floors, water-based is the better choice.
